<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">French Equatorial Africa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Equatorial Africa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">French Equatorial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> was a federation of French colonies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-africa">Central Africa</a>, including present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-african-republic">Central African Republic</a>, Congo and Gabon. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a> was incorporated into it after the French conquest, and it formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> until independence in 1960.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/french-equatorial-africa.jpg" alt="French Equatorial Africa" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ComandanteBruh · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_French_Equatorial_Africa.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
